<HelloFraandsPage title="Refund & cancellation" summary="Call ke paise wapas nahi hote — wallet mein bache hue paise 180 din ke andar Google Play se wapas ho sakte hain." review={true} related={[{"href":"/wallet-terms","label":"Wallet terms"},{"href":"/terms","label":"Terms of use"},{"href":"/grievance","label":"Grievance redressal"}]}>
<h2>No refunds for calls</h2>
<p>{BRAND.name} does not offer refunds for connected calls. You choose the host, you see their per-minute price before you call, and you can hang up at any second, so you are only charged for the connected time you chose to stay on the call.</p>
<h2>We are not responsible for how a call went</h2>
<p>{BRAND.name} connects you with an independent host. We are not responsible for your experience with a particular host, so we cannot refund a call because the conversation was not what you hoped for. Rate the host, try someone else, and <a href="/report">report the host</a> if they broke a rule.</p>
<h2>No connection means no charge</h2>
<p>Billing starts only when both people are connected. Ringing, a host declining, a timeout before connection or a call that fails to connect costs nothing. Calls are billed per started minute of connected time — for example, 61 connected seconds is two minutes — including when either person hangs up, presses # or the call is ended by a safety action.</p>
<h2>Billing errors are corrected</h2>
<p>If you are charged for a call that never connected, or charged twice for the same call, that is a billing error, not a refund request. Report it with the call ID, date and time and it will be checked against the call records and the wrong amount put back in your wallet.</p>
<h2>Your unused balance is always yours</h2>
<p>Unused wallet money can be refunded on request through Google Play within 180 days. This includes accounts that have been banned: a banned account cannot make calls, but can still sign in and request the refund.</p>
<h2>Information for a billing query</h2>
<p>Provide the call ID, date and time, amount, transaction reference and a short explanation, and keep your receipt. Never send an OTP, UPI PIN, Aadhaar number or full card details — we will never ask for them. See the <a href="/grievance">grievance page</a> for how to raise a complaint, and the <a href="/help">help centre</a> for simple guides on the <a href="/help/wallet-and-payments/no-refunds">no-refund rule</a> and <a href="/help/wallet-and-payments/billing-errors">billing mistakes</a>.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
